[API Documentation]
select(input, dim, index) -> Tensor

Slices the :attr:`input` tensor along the selected dimension at the given index.
This function returns a view of the original tensor with the given dimension removed.

.. note:: If :attr:`input` is a sparse tensor and returning a view of
          the tensor is not possible, a RuntimeError exception is
          raised. In this is the case, consider using
          :func:`torch.select_copy` function.

Args:
    input (Tensor): the input tensor.
    dim (int): the dimension to slice
    index (int): the index to select with

.. note::

    :meth:`select` is equivalent to slicing. For example,
    ``tensor.select(0, index)`` is equivalent to ``tensor[index]`` and
    ``tensor.select(2, index)`` is equivalent to ``tensor[:,:,index]``.

[API Signature] input: tensor, dim: integer, index: integer

[Error Messages]
IndexError: select(): index 1 out of range for tensor of size [0] at dimension 0
IndexError: Dimension out of range (expected to be in range of [-1, 0], but got 2)

[Output Format]
Rule {Number} ({Description})\n{Rule Definition}
Ex) Rule 21 (primitive type variable should not be zero)
    {v_1 : int ⊎ float} |= v_1 ≠ 0

[Example Rules]
Rule 14 (tensor should not be empty)
{v_1 : tensor} |= ∀i ∈ [0, ndim(v_1) − 1] : shape(v_1, i) > 0

Rule 9 (4D tensor with all shape dimensions positive)
{v_1 : tensor} |= ndim(v_1) = 4 ∧ ∀i ∈ [0, 3] : shape(v_1, i) > 0

Rule 16 (shape alignment for matrix multiplication)
{v_1 : tensor, v_2 : tensor} |= (ndim(v_1) ≥ 2 ∧ ndim(v_2) ≥ 2 ∧ shape(v_1, ndim(v_1) − 1) = shape(v_2, ndim(v_2) − 2)) ∨ (ndim(v_1) ≥ 2 ∧ ndim(v_2) = 1 ∧ shape(v_1, ndim(v_1) − 1) = shape(v_2, 0))

Rule 2 (v_2 should be a valid dimension of input tensor)
{v_1 : tensor, v_2 : int} |= −1 × ndim(v_1) ≤ v_2 ∧ v_2 ≤ ndim(v_1) − 1

Rule 15 (broadcasting compatibility for tensor shapes)
{v_1 : tensor, v_2 : tensor} |= ndim(v_1) > 0 ∧ ndim(v_2) > 0 ∧ ∀i ∈ [0, if ndim(v_1) ≥ ndim(v_2) then ndim(v_1) − 1 else ndim(v_2) − 1] : ndim(v_1) − i − 1 < 0 ∨ ndim(v_2) − i − 1 < 0 ∨ shape(v_1, ndim(v_1) − i − 1) = 1 ∨ shape(v_2, ndim(v_2) − i − 1) = 1 ∨ shape(v_1, ndim(v_1) − i − 1) = shape(v_2, ndim(v_2) − i − 1)

